From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wine.inf: the Visual C++ runtime and Windows PowerShell are registered

The system has the Visual C++ 2015-2022 runtime (msvcp140, vcruntime140 and the
rest, 14.42.34433, 0636) but not its registration: Transmission 4.1 and Drawpile
2.3 look for VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x64 (Installed, Minor, Version) and
their MSIs ended with 1603 ("The Visual C++ Runtime is not installed"). It is
registered as its redistributable registers itself: x64 in both registry views,
x86 in the 32-bit view. Git Extensions 7.2 looks for Windows PowerShell's
PowerShell\1\ShellIds\Microsoft.PowerShell Path, which every Windows has
(powershell.exe runs PowerShell 7 when installed): PowerShell 1 and 3 are
registered as on Windows 10.

Test: test/sysversions-gate.sh (fails on 10.0-1131).
---
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -183,7 +183,9 @@
     SgDllOverrides,\
     SgAppDefaults,\
     SgKeyboardLayouts,\
-    SgKeyboardLayoutFiles
+    SgKeyboardLayoutFiles,\
+    SgVcRuntime64,\
+    SgPowerShell
 DelReg=SgKeyboardLayoutsGone
 
 [DefaultInstall.ntarm64]
@@ -232,7 +234,10 @@
     VersionInfo,\
     LicenseInformation,\
     SgDllOverrides,\
-    SgAppDefaults
+    SgAppDefaults,\
+    SgVcRuntime64,\
+    SgVcRuntime32,\
+    SgPowerShell
 
 [Wow64Install.ntarm]
 RegisterDlls=RegisterDllsSection
@@ -2870,6 +2875,41 @@
 HKLM,"System\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanmanWorkstation\NetworkProvider","Name",,"Microsoft Windows Network"
 HKLM,"System\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanmanWorkstation\NetworkProvider","ProviderPath",0x20000,"%%SystemRoot%%\System32\ntlanman.dll"
 
+;; Stained Glass OS: the Visual C++ 2015-2022 runtime the system has (msvcp140, vcruntime140 and the
+;; rest are part of it, 14.42.34433, 0636) registered the way its redistributable registers itself.
+;; Installers look for these values before they go on: Transmission's and Drawpile's MSIs ended with
+;; 1603 ("The Visual C++ Runtime is not installed") although the runtime was there. The x64 runtime
+;; is in both registry views, the x86 one in the 32-bit view, as on 64-bit Windows.
+[SgVcRuntime64]
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x64,"Installed",0x10001,1
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x64,"Major",0x10001,14
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x64,"Minor",0x10001,42
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x64,"Bld",0x10001,34433
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x64,"Rbld",0x10001,0
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x64,"Version",,"v14.42.34433.00"
+
+[SgVcRuntime32]
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x86,"Installed",0x10001,1
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x86,"Major",0x10001,14
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x86,"Minor",0x10001,42
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x86,"Bld",0x10001,34433
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x86,"Rbld",0x10001,0
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x86,"Version",,"v14.42.34433.00"
+
+;; Stained Glass OS: Windows PowerShell's registration, as every Windows has it (powershell.exe is in
+;; system32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0 and runs PowerShell 7 when it is installed). Git Extensions' MSI
+;; looks for ShellIds\Microsoft.PowerShell's Path ("This application requires Windows PowerShell").
+[SgPowerShell]
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\PowerShell\1,"Install",0x10001,1
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\PowerShell\1\PowerShellEngine,"ApplicationBase",,"%11%\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0"
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\PowerShell\1\PowerShellEngine,"PowerShellVersion",,"2.0"
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\PowerShell\1\PowerShellEngine,"RuntimeVersion",,"v2.0.50727"
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\PowerShell\1\ShellIds\Microsoft.PowerShell,"Path",,"%11%\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe"
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\PowerShell\3,"Install",0x10001,1
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\PowerShell\3\PowerShellEngine,"ApplicationBase",,"%11%\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0"
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\PowerShell\3\PowerShellEngine,"PowerShellVersion",,"5.1.19041.1"
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\PowerShell\3\PowerShellEngine,"RuntimeVersion",,"v4.0.30319"
+
 [VersionInfo]
 HKLM,%CurrentVersionNT%,"CurrentVersion",2,"6.3"
 HKLM,%CurrentVersionNT%,"CurrentMajorVersionNumber",0x10003,10
